WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
At dawn in Varanasi, pilgrims walk
down stone steps into the Ganges.

2
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:09.240
Hindus call the river
Ganga Ma: Mother Ganga.

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.760
Many believe she came down from heaven.

4
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:15.900
Bathing in her is believed to wash
away the effects of wrongdoing.

5
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:19.440
A holy place like this
is a tirtha: a ford,

6
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.380
a place to cross a river.

7
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.650
So can a river really
wash away wrongdoing?

8
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.100
And can a holy place exist outside India?

9
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:32.480
In this mission, you'll follow the
Ganges from the mountains to Varanasi.

10
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:37.250
Then you'll read why a journey to a holy
place can itself be an act of love for

11
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.350
God.

12
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.730
Your mission: find out what Hindus believe
a holy river and a holy place can do.
